{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Origami → SwiftUI mappings"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow, so the translator","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"targets SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state graph"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — computed properties, ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not imperative functions. Each row below is a rule the codegen applies; the helper","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", …) fills the gaps where a patch has no direct","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftUI equivalent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-four-rules","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The four rules"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftUI","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pure value patch (Add, Transition\/interpolate, logic)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"computed property \/ expression"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Interaction (Tap, Down\/press, Double Tap, Long Press)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"gesture + ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@GestureState"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.drag"},{"text":" — Drag","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"drag(enable:momentum:bounds:position:translation:velocity:reset:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (helper)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State\/memory (Switch, Sample and Hold)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" + update logic","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Animation (Classic Animation, Pop\/Spring)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":".animation(.spring)","type":"codeVoice"}]}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Origami layer tree becomes the SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View"},{"type":"text","text":" body. Origami "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition"},{"type":"text","text":" means"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interpolation (not SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".transition()"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier — that’s a different concept)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Pure-value-patch-%E2%86%92-computed-property","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Pure value patch → computed property"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Add"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition\/interpolate"},{"type":"text","text":", and other pure-function patches carry no state."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They fan an input through math and emit an output. In SwiftUI that’s a computed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property (or an inline expression) — no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", no side effect."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Interaction-%E2%86%92-gesture-+-State","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Interaction → gesture + `@State`"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s Interaction patch exposes discrete output ports: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"down"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"position"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onTap"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onDoubleTap"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onLongPress"},{"type":"text","text":". Each maps to a SwiftUI gesture recognizer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose output lands in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" or fires a callback. The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attaches only the recognizer for each output the caller requests, which keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gesture arbitration clean."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Statememory-%E2%86%92-State-+-update-logic","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"State\/memory → `@State` + update logic"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Switch"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sample and Hold"},{"type":"text","text":" remember a value across evaluations. That’s what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" is for. Codegen emits the state variable plus the update path (a gesture"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"callback, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".onChange"},{"type":"text","text":", or an assignment inside a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" block)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Classic Animation"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pop Animation"},{"text":", and other animation patches drive a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" or an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(_:value:)"},{"text":" modifier on the animated property.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Flag-dont-fake","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Flag, don’t fake"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"absolute-position layout."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"How Swami translates the four kinds of Origami patch into SwiftUI’s state graph.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"],"anchor":"Reference","generated":true}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings"]}],"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction","abstract":[{"text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Interaction","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" patch.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","kind":"symbol","title":"Interaction","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction"}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Drag":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drag","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/drag","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Drag","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Drag","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Drag"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" patch (","type":"text"},{"code":"origami.Drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Beats":{"type":"topic","title":"Beats","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/beats","abstract":[{"text":"The four-beat discipline that keeps the translator honest: one pattern per branch,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compile-clean before opening a PR, visual gate against Origami’s own render, ship","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only on Reviewer approval plus a human spot-check.","type":"text"}],"role":"article"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"url":"\/documentation\/swami","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"Swami","role":"collection"}}}